            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ūrō, ūrere — \"to burn; to scorch\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sōl agrōs ūrēbat. The sun was scorching the fields."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ūrō, ūrere, ussī, ustum. It has many compounds; English combustion comes from combūrō."
            }
          ]
        },
