          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ūrō is an inherited verb; Lewis & Short compare Greek heuō, \"to singe\". English combustion comes from its compound combūrō."
