              "text": "flagrō, flagrāre — \"to blaze, to be on fire\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Domus flagrābat, et vīcīnī aquam portābant. The house was blazing, and the neighbours were carrying water."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "flagrō, flagrāre, flagrāvī: to blaze, and of people, to burn with a feeling. English flagrant."
            }
          ]
        },
